## Part 1: Who Anvith Is

### The Real Story

Anvith joined GlobusIT in late 2024 as a Data Analyst. His first observation: field worker data for a state government telecom project (T-Fiber) was being collected through WhatsApp. A communication app. Not a data system. Nobody asked him to fix this. He identified the gap, taught himself Google Apps Script, built a collection system, automated the reporting hierarchy, and kept going.

Two months after joining, management promoted him to Junior PM. Not because he lobbied for it. Because they watched him plan a product, build it completely alone, document it with BRDs and ERDs and user flow documents, train field employees across eight districts, collect feedback, and ship updates — all while doing his original job.

By March 2025 he has ten shipped or near-shipped products. Two Indian states. 152 employees tracked. ₹0 in infrastructure costs across all systems. Every product built solo. Every product documented before a line of code was written.

He migrated himself from Google Apps Script to React 18 to Next.js 16 not through tutorials — through production systems built under real constraints for real government contracts. Each technology was learned by shipping something that required it.

He says this about himself: "I can fix it and I can make it work as a product." That sentence is the complete philosophy. Not perfectionism about implementation. Total commitment to outcome.

### The Three Things This Portfolio Proves

**1. The builder instinct is real.** He does not wait to be asked. He sees gaps other people accept as permanent. The WhatsApp-to-production migration is documented here. So are nine other products built on the same instinct.

**2. The PM discipline existed before the title.** Every product has BRDs, ERDs, and atomic user flow documentation. The December 2024 promotion made official something that was already happening.

**3. The trajectory is steep and accelerating.** Google Apps Script → React → Next.js → Supabase → Prisma → real-time systems. Each project is harder than the last. The arc visible in the portfolio is more impressive than any credential.

### The Thesis

Every visitor should understand this within ten seconds of landing:

**"Promoted to Junior PM in two months. For building ten products nobody asked for."**

That sentence is true. It is specific. It is impossible to fake. The entire portfolio is the evidence.

