## Part 11: Technical Architecture

### Philosophy

Next.js 14, App Router, TypeScript strict mode throughout. Production code quality — because this portfolio is itself evidence of Anvith's technical judgment, and that judgment is visible in how the code is organized.

### Content System

**Products:** One MDX file per product. Frontmatter contains structured data. MDX body contains case study narrative. Adding a product is one file.

**Config JSON files:** `status.json` (building/reading/available), `metrics.json` (impact numbers), `timeline.json` (career events). Updated by editing one file, no framework required.

No CMS. Anvith is comfortable with code editors. A CMS adds maintenance overhead without adding capability for a solo developer managing their own portfolio.

### API Integrations

**Anthropic Claude API (claude-sonnet-4-6)** — the chat assistant. Streaming via SSE. Ten queries per session, rate-limited in Supabase.

**Supabase** — contact form submissions, chat rate limiting, session analytics, visitor presence.

**GitHub API** — last deployment timestamp, contribution heatmap.

**Resend** — contact form email notifications.

Every integration has a documented graceful fallback. If any service is unavailable, the portfolio looks and functions correctly.

### Performance

Every page feels instant on a standard Indian mobile connection. Lighthouse Performance above 90 on every core route.

The dot grid is pure CSS — zero JavaScript cost.  
Heavy visualizations load lazily, never blocking first render.  
AI chat is loaded dynamically with `ssr: false`.  
All images served at the appropriate size for the device via proper `sizes` prop.  
No images without explicit dimensions (eliminates layout shift).  
No font loading layout shift (next/font with display:swap, preloaded weights only).

